{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Valliya (2nd)","html":"<article id='thag2.3'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.3 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.3 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Paṭhamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter One </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Valliyattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Valliya (2nd) </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Makkaṭo pañcadvārāyaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A monkey went up to the little hut </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kuṭikāyaṁ pasakkiya; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>with five doors. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dvārena anupariyeti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>He circles around, knocking </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ghaṭṭayanto muhuṁ muhuṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>on each door, again and again. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tiṭṭha makkaṭa mā dhāvi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stand still monkey, don’t run! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>na hi te taṁ yathā pure; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Things are different now; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Niggahītosi paññāya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you’ve been caught by wisdom—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>neva dūraṁ gamissatī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you won’t go far. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Valliyo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
